    "body": "pulse task #2837 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:6e6efe502ea632ad493eac4dc7540d8f -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2837: Add Rename Track to the track context menu\n\nOperation: 6e6efe502ea632ad493eac4dc7540d8f\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nUser requests Rename Track in the track's right-click context menu. Reuse existing #2768/merged PR376 inline Command-R editor and canonical rename/history behavior, including current text case presentation/selection. No new naming state or separate modal. Menu action operates on the actual right-clicked track identity even if another track was selected; do not accidentally rename the previous selection or retarget after menu opens. Label Rename Track with Command-R hint where existing menu styling supports it. Dismiss menu, focus the existing inline name editor, and preserve existing Enter commit/Escape cancel, text/IME shortcut isolation, Undo/Redo/save/reopen. Applicable normal/Return rows should use existing supported naming commands; report any unsupported Main/special row rather than inventing semantics. Cancel/dismiss or deleted/stale menu target is a safe no-op.\n\nDuplicate check found only completed2768 keyboard rename, no focused context-menu request. Coordinate existing #2834/PR438 same menu's Insert Track/Insert Return actions and source2 #2826/430 generic context-menu grid metadata; preserve all actions and exact owner hunks, no whole-file replacement or second writer. Source1 owns shared track/header menu; queue after essential Open/device-focus coherent checkpoint, smallest focused PR and actual right-click->Rename->target/commit/cancel test. No broad new UI framework or track creation/type/routing change. Targeted local checks and immutable handoff to sole merger; In Progress while unmerged, Ready for Review only after actual merge. Root owns native acceptance, no live user-app actions.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
